# Defect 457 and panel 199's R1, ratified 2026-10-09: the message the blind
# seat read, whole. A call written `x.f()` is told that `x.f(y)` is `f(x, y)`,
# which is how the author meets the shape (defect 455's `bytes`); every
# refusal names the ways out a path may take before the call, and says that
# an abort nobody wrote is none of them. No fix: which path should return,
# and what, are the author's to say.

function bytes(s: str) -> [u8]
    return s.bytes()  #~ endless_recursion

function fact(n: i64) -> i64
    return n * fact(n - 1)  #~ endless_recursion

function main()
    print(bytes("hi").len())
    print(fact(5))
